course: dictionary
lesson: 547
title: Attacker, in danger and in sport
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An attacker is a person or animal that attacks someone. In a news story, «The attacker ran off», and «Tell police what the attacker looked like» are about danger. Context clues like ran off and police tell you the meaning fits.
explain: In sport, an attacker is a player whose job is to score goals or points. «In soccer the offside rule stops attackers waiting by the goal» shows they are the players who try to score, not the ones who defend. Ask what word would fit: a striker or forward fits, a goalkeeper does not.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. Read the words around attacker to find the right one. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «the attacker fled» or «the star attacker scored» still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: An attacker is a person or animal that attacks someone.
fact: In sport, an attacker is a player whose job is to score goals or points.
fact: Attackers is the plural: one attacker, many attackers.
fact: Useful phrases: «the attacker fled», «fight off an attacker», and «star attacker».
fact: In «Porcupines cannot shoot their quills», the quills stick into the attacker when touched, which helps the porcupine defend itself.
exercise: «Tell the police what the attacker looked like.» What is an attacker here? | A shop worker who sells the tickets | A police officer | *A person or animal that attacks someone | A player who scores goals
exercise: «In soccer the offside rule stops attackers waiting by the goal.» In sport, what does attacker mean? | *A player whose job is to score goals or points | A goalkeeper who stops shots | A referee who blows the whistle | A coach who picks the team
exercise: «The star attacker scored three goals.» Which word in the sentence tells you the meaning is about sport? | three | the | star | *scored
test: «Many lizards can drop their tail on purpose; it wriggles to distract the attacker.» What is the attacker? | *An animal or person that attacks the lizard | A kind of wriggling worm | A bird that flies over the lizard | The lizard's new tail
test: Which sentence uses attacker to mean a sports player? | *The attacker dived in front of the goal and headed the ball in. | Porcupines stick their quills into an attacker. | Tell the police what the attacker looked like. | The attacker ran off down the street after the bag was taken.
exam: Jayden says an attacker can only ever be a person. Is he right? | Yes, but only in sport | No, because attackers are always goalkeepers | Yes, only people can be attackers | *No, an animal, like a porcupine, can be an attacker too
